Let's plug $\blueD{a=-8}$, $\maroonD{b=-2}$, and $\purpleC{h(x)=\dfrac{x^3+7x^2+3}{2x^2-5x+4}}$ into the formula:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{\displaystyle\int_{\blueD a}^{\maroonD b} \purpleC{h(x)}\,dx}{\maroonD b-\blueD a}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\displaystyle\int_{\blueD {-8}}^{\maroonD{-2}} \purpleC{\dfrac{x^3+7x^2+3}{2x^2-5x+4}}\,dx}{\maroonD{-2}-(\blueD{-8})}
\\\\
&=\dfrac16\displaystyle\int_{-8}^{-2} \dfrac{x^3+7x^2+3}{2x^2-5x+4}\,dx
\end{align}$
